WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.980
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Size of the Problem.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:19.961
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:19.961 --> 00:00:23.549
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.549 --> 00:00:27.137
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:35.510
Problems are not all the same size. A dropped crayon and a hurt friend are both problems — but they are not the same size of problem.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:45.079
Reactions come in sizes too. A sigh is one size. Tears are another. A shout is another.

00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:55.844
The work — the whole work of this tool — is matching: the size of the reaction to the size of the problem.

00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:00.628
Let me show you the sizes.

00:01:00.628 --> 00:01:11.393
Small problems: I can try a fix. A dropped crayon — pick it up. A page that won't turn — try again, slowly.

00:01:11.393 --> 00:01:22.158
Medium problems: I need a classmate, or a strategy. A tower that keeps falling. A turn that feels unfair. Help nearby is the move.

00:01:22.158 --> 00:01:32.922
Big problems: a grown-up, right away. And here is the rule that never changes: anything unsafe is automatically big.

00:01:32.922 --> 00:01:42.491
If anyone could get hurt — body or heart — the problem is big, and a grown-up is the move. Every time. No sizing first.

00:01:42.491 --> 00:01:43.687
Naming the size is not the finish. The size just tells your body which move comes next.

00:01:43.687 --> 00:01:54.452
Now hear this part with both ears: if a small problem gets a big reaction, that reaction is never wrong, bad, or too much.

00:01:54.452 --> 00:02:05.217
A big reaction is information. It may mean something else is riding along — a hard morning, a tired body, an older worry.

00:02:05.217 --> 00:02:13.590
Feelings themselves never get a size. Sad is not small. Angry is not big. Only problems and reactions get sizes — never feelings.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.786
And nobody sizes perfectly. Not you, not me, not grown-ups. Matching is a practice, and practice is allowed to be wobbly.

00:02:14.786 --> 00:02:23.158
Name the size. Choose the move. That is the match.

00:02:23.158 --> 00:02:29.139
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:29.139 --> 00:02:33.923
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:39.904
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:39.904 --> 00:02:45.884
You're ready for what's next.
